  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ADDRESSING HUMAN-WILDLIFE CONFLICT INVOLVING EASTERN CHIMPANZEES (PAN TROGLODYTES SCHWEINFURTHII) IN THE BUDONGO-BUGOMA LANDSCAPE OF THE ALBERTINE RIFT, UGANDA</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">THE PURPOSE OF THIS PROJECT IS TO PROMOTE COEXISTENCE BETWEEN HUMANS AND ENDANGERED EASTERN CHIMPANZEES IN WESTERN UGANDA S BUDONGO-BUGOMA LANDSCAPE BY: (1) IMPROVING MONITORING OF HUMAN-CHIMPANZEE CONFLICT (2) INCREASING AWARENESS AND CAPACITY OF PRIVATE FOREST OWNERS ASSOCIATIONS TO MITIGATE HUMAN-WILDLIFE CONFLICT, INCLUDING USE OF UNPALATABLE CROPS AND LIVE FENCES AND (3) ESTABLISHING VILLAGE SAVINGS AND LOAN ASSOCIATIONS TO PROVIDE A SUSTAINABLE, COMMUNITY-DRIVEN FINANCE MECHANISM TO SUPPORT HUMAN-WILDLIFE CONFLICT MITIGATION ACTIVITIES.</narrative>
  </description>
